{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"blousy-luxuriant-rasbora","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Operator directive (verbatim, 2026-08-13)\n'add that alongside our existing portability invariant as an agent guidance rule for this project: keeping rebar portable means it working across environments with diverse CI providers or no CI provider.'\n\n## Context\nDiscovered via the compaction redesign: story A removed the operation-linked compaction trigger and story B initially replaced it with a GitHub-Actions-only schedule — a design that silently breaks adopters with no CI. The operator's constraint ('compaction needs to work in environments without local cron and CI') generalizes to a project invariant.\n\n## Work\n- Locate the EXISTING portability invariant statement(s): the project.portability review criterion (its definition/detection text — check .rebar/criteria_routing.json and the criteria registry/docs) and any docs statement (docs/ci-provider-matrix.md is adjacent).\n- Add the rule alongside it, stated as agent guidance: rebar features must function across environments with diverse CI providers or NO CI provider; a capability whose only trigger is a specific CI system is not portable — operation-linked or in-process fallbacks are required.\n- Surface it where agents actually read: AGENTS.md (the canonical agent guidance — keep it to a lean bullet per that file's own rules) and the project.portability criterion's detection detail so plan reviews enforce it.\n- Cross-link, don't triplicate.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] AGENTS.md carries the rule as a concise agent-guidance bullet.\n- [ ] The project.portability criterion's detection text covers the no-CI-provider case so a plan whose only trigger is a specific CI system draws a finding.\n- [ ] docs cross-reference rather than restate (one authoritative wording).","id":"ce7d-3a15-51e5-4c6a","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Portability guidance: diverse CI providers or none"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786614082177257001,"uuid":"c1959201-d7eb-4ca4-abd5-ac1ec339a904"}